  "summary_text": "Falcon (payments migration)\nSam confirmed he owns Falcon (PAY-212)\nRisks and test fixtures and backfill job\nRisks is a bit of a black box\nTest fixtures is a little fragile\nBackfill job is basically done\nPreference to draw it on a whiteboard rather than cut the scope\nCaching layer and logging format and pagination bug\nCaching layer is a moving target\nCaching layer is in good shape\nOpen question: what the plan is for logging format\nLogging format is not where i'd want it\nPagination bug is in a weird spot\nSuggestion to do a quick spike before touching pagination bug\nFeedback on pagination bug from the new folks: they had a lot of opinions\nPreference to keep it behind a flag rather than start with the boring version\nError budget and requirements and linting rules\nConcern with error budget: that it creates more support load\nOpen question: what the plan is for requirements\nLinting rules is mostly cosmetic\nPreference to keep it behind a flag rather than look at it with fresh eyes\nNext steps\nSam to write the Falcon cutover script by Thursday\nRuth to set up the device lab for Otter by Friday\nAlex to finish the backend job description by Wednesday\nSam to add idempotency keys to the webhook handler by Wednesday",
  "summary_markdown": "### Falcon (payments migration)\n- Sam confirmed he owns Falcon (PAY-212)\n\n### Risks and test fixtures and backfill job\n- Risks is a bit of a black box\n- Test fixtures is a little fragile\n- Backfill job is basically done\n- Preference to draw it on a whiteboard rather than cut the scope\n\n### Caching layer and logging format and pagination bug\n- Caching layer is a moving target\n  - Caching layer is in good shape\n- Open question: what the plan is for logging format\n  - Logging format is not where i'd want it\n- Pagination bug is in a weird spot\n  - Suggestion to do a quick spike before touching pagination bug\n  - Feedback on pagination bug from the new folks: they had a lot of opinions\n- Preference to keep it behind a flag rather than start with the boring version\n\n### Error budget and requirements and linting rules\n- Concern with error budget: that it creates more support load\n- Open question: what the plan is for requirements\n- Linting rules is mostly cosmetic\n- Preference to keep it behind a flag rather than look at it with fresh eyes\n\n### Next steps\n- Sam to write the Falcon cutover script by **Thursday**\n- Ruth to set up the device lab for Otter by **Friday**\n- Alex to finish the backend job description by **Wednesday**\n- Sam to add idempotency keys to the webhook handler by **Wednesday**",
  "private_notes_text": null,
  "private_notes_markdown": null,
